## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical serverless design, idempotency, error handling, and IAM least privilege in a real-world image workflow.

## Key Concepts

- S3 event triggers and Lambda integration
- Idempotent design using a dedupe key stored in DynamoDB
- Least-privilege IAM roles for S3, Lambda, and DynamoDB
- Dead Letter Queue (DLQ) setup for failed events

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal idempotent Lambda outline
const AWS = require('aws-sdk');
const ddb = new AWS.DynamoDB.DocumentClient();
// image processing omitted
exports.handler = async (event) => {
  const rec = event.Records[0];
  const key = recs.s3.object.key;
  const jobKey = key;
  const exists = await ddb.get({TableName:'processed', Key:{jobKey}}).promise();
  if (exists.Item) return {status:'skipped'};
  // resize and store output placeholder
  await ddb.put({TableName:'processed', Item:{jobKey, t: Date.now()}}).promise();
  return {status:'done'};
};
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test idempotency under concurrent uploads?
- How would you monitor DLQ failures and ensure timely retries?

